From c6d0d3f007fef2dee981f16f74a128eb4a6265a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:27:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_conv: a constant signed integer to float cast
 sign-extends its source

librsvg 2.58.5 (the Rust librsvg port): rsvg-convert wrote fully transparent PNGs. RSVG_LOG=1
showed, for every element of every file (a plain <rect> too):

    will not render rect id=None: path has coordinates that are unsuitable for Cairo

rsvg/src/path_builder.rs checks each transformed point against the range Cairo's fixed-point
numbers can hold, `CAIRO_FIXED_MIN_DOUBLE..=CAIRO_FIXED_MAX_DOUBLE`, from float_eq_cairo.rs:

    const CAIRO_FIXED_ONE_DOUBLE: f64 = (1 << CAIRO_FIXED_FRAC_BITS) as f64;
    pub const CAIRO_FIXED_MAX_DOUBLE: f64 = (CAIRO_FIXED_MAX as f64) / CAIRO_FIXED_ONE_DOUBLE;
    pub const CAIRO_FIXED_MIN_DOUBLE: f64 = (CAIRO_FIXED_MIN as f64) / CAIRO_FIXED_ONE_DOUBLE;  // i32::MIN

Constant evaluation of a `signed as float` cast read the source with read_uint (zero-extended)
and only then made it an S128, so `i32::MIN as f64` was +2147483648.0, CAIRO_FIXED_MIN_DOUBLE
+8388608.0, the range 8388608.0..=8388607.99 empty, and no point was ever inside it. Every
negative constant cast to f32/f64 was affected (`-5i32 as f64` = 4294967291.0, `-5i8` = 251.0),
on every target; run-time casts are C casts and were right. The source is now read with
read_sint, as the integer-to-integer arm already did.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context)
---

diff --git a/src/hir_conv/constant_evaluation.cpp b/src/hir_conv/constant_evaluation.cpp
index c7fca7ac..1cf75046 100644
--- a/src/hir_conv/constant_evaluation.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_conv/constant_evaluation.cpp
@@ -2244,7 +2244,8 @@ namespace HIR {
                     {
                     // NOTE: Subtle rounding differences between f32 and f64
                     case TypeInfo::Signed: {
-                        auto v = S128(inval.read_uint(state, src_ti.bits));
+                        // Sign-extended: `read_uint` made `-5i32 as f64` 4294967291.0
+                        auto v = inval.read_sint(state, src_ti.bits);
                         dst.write_float(state, ti.bits, ti.bits == 32 ? v.to_float() : v.to_double() );
                         break; }
                     case TypeInfo::Unsigned: {
